- entry .j   the `j"…"` interpolator: a JSON literal checked as it compiles, with holes, spreads and merges
-     `j"""{"a": $x}"""` is a `Json` whose syntax was checked while the code compiled — a
-     trailing comma, say, is reported at the character — and whose holes are filled at runtime.
-     A hole substitutes any value `Encodable in Json`; inside an array, `$xs*` splices every
-     element of a collection; among an object's fields, a `$map` hole merges a `Map[Text, Json]`.
-     In a `match`, the same interpolator is a pattern which binds its holes.
+ entry .j   el interpolador `j"…"`: un literal JSON comprobado al compilar, con huecos, expansiones y fusiones
+     `j"""{"a": $x}"""` es un `Json` cuya sintaxis se comprobó al compilar el código —una coma
+     final, por ejemplo, se señala en el carácter— y cuyos huecos se rellenan en tiempo de
+     ejecución. Un hueco sustituye cualquier valor `Encodable in Json`; dentro de un array,
+     `$xs*` inserta todos los elementos de una colección; entre los campos de un objeto, un
+     hueco `$map` fusiona un `Map[Text, Json]`. En un `match`, el mismo interpolador es un patrón
+     que vincula sus huecos.

=     In a `match`, the same interpolator is a pattern which binds its holes.
=
-     ```scala
+     ```scala

=     In a `match`, the same interpolator is a pattern which binds its holes.
=
=     ```scala
-     import soundness.*
+     import soundness.*

-     val x = 42
+     val x = 42

-     val xs = List(2, 3, 4)
+     val xs = List(2, 3, 4)

-     val rest: Map[Text, Json] = Map(t"b" -> 2.in[Json], t"c" -> 3.in[Json])
+     val rest: Map[Text, Json] = Map(t"b" -> 2.in[Json], t"c" -> 3.in[Json])

-     j"""{"a": $x}"""         // {"a": 42}
+     j"""{"a": $x}"""         // {"a": 42}

-     j"""[1, $xs*]"""         // [1, 2, 3, 4]
+     j"""[1, $xs*]"""         // [1, 2, 3, 4]

-     j"""{"a": 1, $rest}"""   // {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3}
+     j"""{"a": 1, $rest}"""   // {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3}

-     j"""[1, 2, 3, 4]""" match
+     j"""[1, 2, 3, 4]""" match

-       case j"""[$head, $tail*]""" => (head, tail)
+       case j"""[$head, $tail*]""" => (head, tail)

-       case _                      => (j"0", j"[]")
+       case _                      => (j"0", j"[]")

-     j""" {"a": 1, } """   // does not compile: a trailing comma
+     j""" {"a": 1, } """   // does not compile: a trailing comma

=     j""" {"a": 1, } """   // does not compile: a trailing comma
-     ```
+     ```

